-- title:
--   Cyclotomic levels prime to a finite bad set are disjoint from F
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field and let $\Omega$ be a field equipped with a $K$-algebra structure (no further assumption: $\Omega$ need not be algebraic over $K$ nor contain roots of unity). Let $F$ be an intermediate field of $\Omega/K$ that is finite-dimensional over $K$. The assertion is that there exists a finite set $B_0$ of natural numbers such that every element of $B_0$ is prime, and such that for every natural number $m$ with $m \neq 0$, every $\zeta \in \Omega$ which is a primitive $m$-th root of unity, and under the hypothesis that no prime factor of $m$ belongs to $B_0$, one has
--   $$[\,F \sqcup K(\zeta) : K\,] = [F : K]\cdot \varphi(m),$$
--   where $F \sqcup K(\zeta)$ is the join of $F$ with the $K$-subalgebra-closure $K(\zeta)$ generated by $\zeta$ in the lattice of intermediate fields of $\Omega/K$, i.e. the compositum of $F$ and $K(\zeta)$ inside $\Omega$, degrees are $K$-dimensions as modules, and $\varphi$ is Euler's totient. The order of quantifiers matters: the set $B_0$ is chosen once and for all in terms of $K$, $\Omega$ and $F$, and then serves simultaneously for every level $m$ prime to it and every primitive $m$-th root of unity of that level in $\Omega$.
--
--   This is the linear disjointness, over a number field $K$, of a fixed finite extension $F$ from the cyclotomic extensions $K(\zeta_m)$ of level $m$ prime to a finite set of ramified primes attached to $F$; a set that works consists of the primes dividing the absolute discriminant of $F$. It is used in the Artin-representation part of the Langlands–Tunnell input, where a cyclotomic level must be chosen so as not to increase the degree of a prescribed field of definition, and is cited by the constructions of the field and pair data underlying that step.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LanglandsTunnell_Artin_exists_badPrimes_finrank_sup_adjoin_eq_mul_totient.lean

import Mathlib.NumberTheory.NumberField.Basic
import Mathlib.RingTheory.RootsOfUnity.PrimitiveRoots

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v

theorem LanglandsTunnell.Artin.exists_badPrimes_finrank_sup_adjoin_eq_mul_totient
    {K : Type u} [Field K] [NumberField K] {Ω : Type v} [Field Ω] [Algebra K Ω]
    (F : IntermediateField K Ω) [FiniteDimensional K F] :
    ∃ B₀ : Finset ℕ, (∀ p ∈ B₀, p.Prime) ∧
      ∀ (m : ℕ) [NeZero m] (ζ : Ω), IsPrimitiveRoot ζ m → (∀ p ∈ m.primeFactors, p ∉ B₀) →
        Module.finrank K ↥(F ⊔ IntermediateField.adjoin K {ζ}) = Module.finrank K F * m.totient := by sorry
